X:2
T:Konpira fune fune
T:Japanese game song
C:traditional (Japan)
O:Japan, Kagawa (Kotohira)
R:hand-game song
S:Nagai Iwai and Obata Kenhachiro (eds.), 1895, via Daisyfield.com transcription (Tom Potter, 2008, donated to the public domain)
N:A party hand game from Kotohira, home of the Konpira shrine: two players face each other across a small stand and touch it in turn, in time to the song, which goes faster each time round; a player who hesitates or touches out of turn is out. The melody is given without words, as in the transcription; the words are to be added once checked against Nagai and Obata. The tune is built on the yo scale on G (G A C D E, with one passing F in bar 12) and ends on G, so the band holds an open fifth on G (G5) rather than changing chords.
Q:1/4=112
M:2/4
L:1/8
K:C
